    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "CBPM Real Estate is delighted to bring to the market this well-presented two-bedroom, one-bathroom semi-detached bungalow, ideally located at 34 Coolagary, Walsh Island, Geashill, Co. Offaly, R35 HP58. Built in 1976, the property extends to approximately 67.06 sq. m. (722 sq. ft.), has a BER rating of D and benefits from gas heating. Offering comfortable single-storey accommodation together with an exceptionally generous rear garden, covered outdoor entertaining area and detached shed, this property is an ideal opportunity for first-time buyers, downsizers or those seeking a manageable home with excellent outdoor space.\n\nThe living area is bright and comfortable, with a wood-burning stove providing an attractive focal point against a feature stone-effect wall. The room flows naturally through to the dining and kitchen area, creating a practical and sociable living space.\n\nThe kitchen is a particularly attractive feature of the home, with a striking vaulted ceiling and exposed timber beams creating a wonderful sense of height and character. There is a good range of fitted units and worktop space together with a breakfast bar, while the large window provides plenty of natural light and views towards the rear garden.\n\nThe property comprises two well-proportioned bedrooms, both offering comfortable accommodation, with space for wardrobe storage.\n\nThe bathroom is fitted with a shower enclosure, WC and wash-hand basin, with a large window providing natural light and ventilation.\n\nOutside is where this property really comes into its own. To the front, the bungalow is set behind timber fencing with a neat lawn, while a gravelled driveway to the side provides convenient off-street parking and access towards the rear.\n\nA substantial covered outdoor area provides an excellent sheltered space for outdoor dining and entertaining, allowing the garden to be enjoyed throughout much of the year. A detached shed offers useful additional storage.\n\nBeyond this lies a surprisingly large and well-maintained rear garden, predominantly laid in lawn and bordered by established hedging and fencing. Gravel pathways wind through sections of the garden, while a dedicated seating and firepit area creates an inviting spot for relaxing outdoors. The garden also includes a polytunnel, offering excellent scope for anyone interested in growing their own fruit and vegetables.\n\n34 Coolagary offers an appealing combination of comfortable bungalow living and an unusually generous outdoor space. With its characterful kitchen, wood-burning stove, off-street parking, covered entertaining area, shed and extensive rear garden, this is a home with plenty to offer its next owner.\n\nAccommodation\n\nOpen Plan Living Room/Dining/Kitchen 3.10m x 11.19 Laminate flooring, recessed lighting, light fittings, solid fuel stove, fully fitted kitchen, fited electric oven and hob, blind, hob extractor\nBedroom 1 2.95m x 3.23m Carpet, recessed lighting, fitted wardrobe, curtain pole\nBathroom 2.92m x 1.08m Carpet, recessed lighting, fitted wardrobe, curtain pole\nBedroom 2 3.66m x 4.44 Carpet, recessed lighting, curtain pole\nPatio 3.43m x 6.50m - Concrete, fitted counter\nShed 3.43m x 5.75m\n"
      },
